        designLead: "Saket Adhikarla",
        qualityLead: "",
        v2momMethod: "Slack",
        version: "slack",
        details: {
            overview: "Please read Link Callout: The architecture decision needs to be aligned among Sales Cloud, Slack and Revenue Cloud. The goal for this epic is to get the MVP goals work with the design choice, and implement and test the quoting use cases. The epic needs to capture the pre-req for being qualified as monthly release candidate, ensure any necessary data model and complex service changes are done. The work needs to be gated. Summary: Enable Revenue Agents (Rev agents) to be productive in Slack via Agentforce integrations: notification routing, quick actions (view quote, Q2O, create opportunity, create simple quote, submit for approval, summarization, generate docs), and a Slack agent that can summarize revenue related elements like approval status and suggest comments, products, upselling opportunities. Key goals (short): Allow revenue agents to perform existing and new tasks via slackbot Provide Rev agents with a Slack-driven workflow to triage approvals and reply with recommended comments. Support sharing of quote previews, approval comments generation, and routing to queues. Include ergonomics: commands, slash-command, and bot dialogs. Deliverables (short): Slack agent flows and recommended prompts Approved for comment generation Integration with approval templates and admin controls",
            keyFeatures: [],
            impact: "[2026-06-03] \"Overall Status: Green 🟢\n\nOther Progress : \n1. No work was slotted for this week\"\n\n[2026-06-10] \"Overall Status: Green 🟢 w/ Callout\n\nCallout:\n- This has been deprioritized for 264 to make room for Slack for Revenue(RevFlow) initiative\n\nPath to Green:\n- N/A, as this will be re-evaluated for 266\n\nOther Progress :\n1. None\"\n\n[2026-06-22] Callout:\n- This has been deprioritized for 264 to make room for Slack for Revenue(RevFlow) initiative\n\n[2026-07-14] \"Overall Status: Green 🟢\n\nOther Progress : \n1. Blitz completed this week\n2. Next week will focus on closing out bugs, automation, instrumentation \""
        },
